                                "sense_id": "03e43b8b-b39d-36b9-a45f-afb56f044fe8",
                                "text": "The peculiar strength of popular music (and, by analogy, civil poetry) is that it is a public utterance capable of connecting with hearers who are in danger of becoming lost in private confusion; that is, they may wander in wonderlands or neverlands of private neuroses, often sexual."
